  "assumptions": [
    "Idealized bar proxy: 09:59 close signal, 15:30 open entry, 15:59 close exit, prior close = last minute bar before the preceding session's official close (12:59 on early closes).",
    "Costs 1 bp/side base (verdict) and 2 bp/side stress (reported only).",
    "100% of after-tax equity per trade, zero return on idle cash, fractional sizing ceiling.",
    "24% of each calendar year's positive net realized P&L debited after its last session; no loss benefit or carryforward; terminal partial year taxed at the end.",
    "CAGR = (W_end/W_0)^(1/y) - 1, y = days(anchor -> last)/365.25.",
    "SPY benchmark: same close-bar prices from the anchor, cash distributions from the issuer schedule (dividend plus any capital-gain legs present; a blank leg is no data, not zero) reinvested at the ex-date session close, no tax; the ex-dividend-flat diagnostic zeroes every issuer distribution ex-date. The rule's own returns use raw prices.",
    "Issuer amounts are assumed USD per share. Alpaca cash dividends are a non-gating cross-check at 6 decimal places (recorded in the validation artifact).",
    "R1: 2019-08-12 and 2019-08-13 are removed from the scored series, not scored as flat days, so every statistic below uses the validated sessions only; the CAGR year count, window and tax-ledger rules are unchanged. The close-convention comparison also leaves out both sessions. The SPY buy-and-hold comparison is not interrupted: it holds through both sessions and earns their price moves, because a continuous hold cannot drop a day without inventing a cash gap (r9 keeps the r8 comparison unchanged). Only the missing 2019-08-12 valuation point is absent from its path; the comparison is non-gating.",
    "Losing streak counts consecutive losing traded sessions; flat sessions are skipped.",
    "Worst month and drawdown use the pre-tax base-cost sleeve.",
    "Hit rate is the share of traded sessions with a positive net return.",
    "No in-window SPY split or unsupported action appeared in the corporate-actions response (same-ticker SPY name changes are counted metadata); that response is not certified complete. The vendor-adjustment review is a bounded documentation review bound by hash, not proof that no undocumented change exists (see ancillary_coverage).",
